# ── Build output ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/target
/dist
**/*.rs.bk
*.pending-snap
web/__pycache__/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
# The client's CDN dependencies, downloaded by the image build (see
# web/tools/vendor.py). Ninety-nine generated files that belong to a pin list,
# not to history — and a copy left here would shadow nothing, because the build
# ignores it too.
web/vendor/

# Test-suite reports (testsuite/run.sh writes one directory per lane).
/testsuite/out/

# ── AI / agent working files ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Local instruction files, session state and the scratch notes agents
# leave behind. These are working files and are not distributed with the
# project. Excluding a path here is a packaging decision only: it makes
# no statement about the terms the distributed source is offered under,
# which are stated in one place and nowhere else.
CLAUDE.md
CLAUDE.local.md
.claude/
.claude.json
AGENTS.md
AGENT.md
GEMINI.md
.gemini/
.cursorrules
.cursor/
